WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.667
Self healing UI automation.

2
00:00:02.967 --> 00:00:06.451
A designer reorders a page, and your whole suite goes red.

3
00:00:06.451 --> 00:00:08.733
The login button is still right there.

4
00:00:09.933 --> 00:00:12.233
Compare two ways to click the login button.

5
00:00:12.533 --> 00:00:15.733
The brittle way uses a CSS path with a position.

6
00:00:15.733 --> 00:00:18.400
It breaks the moment the layout changes.

7
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:23.467
The resilient way uses the role and the visible name, so refactors don't matter.

8
00:00:23.767 --> 00:00:25.800
That targets meaning, not structure.

9
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.200
Self healing tools go further and rank several signals.

10
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:32.533
Visible text, and the ARIA role.

11
00:00:32.833 --> 00:00:34.667
Relative position on the page.

12
00:00:34.967 --> 00:00:37.100
What the element looks like in a screenshot.

13
00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:39.463
And which selector worked last time.

14
00:00:39.463 --> 00:00:42.100
Many weak signals beat one brittle strong one.

15
00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.500
Then the tool must decide how sure it is.

16
00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:48.533
With high confidence, it heals and continues.

17
00:00:48.833 --> 00:00:53.227
With low confidence, it fails loudly and flags the test for a human.

18
00:00:53.227 --> 00:00:56.200
A confidence floor beats a silent wrong click.

19
00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.900
In code, the resilient baseline is simple.

20
00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:04.800
The first line depends on component classes and position, so it breaks easily.

21
00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:09.400
The second asks for a button named Log in, exactly what a user would see.

22
00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:11.933
Here is a real case.

23
00:01:12.233 --> 00:01:16.033
A rebrand changes the component library behind every button.

24
00:01:16.333 --> 00:01:21.067
The forty percent of the suite using structural CSS locators goes red.

25
00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:25.051
The half already using role based locators passes untouched.

26
00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:27.200
That's the poor man's self healing.

27
00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:29.173
Let's recap.

28
00:01:29.173 --> 00:01:31.300
Locate by meaning, not structure.

29
00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:33.533
Rank several weak signals together.

30
00:01:33.833 --> 00:01:35.167
Set a confidence floor.

31
00:01:35.467 --> 00:01:38.333
And fail loud, never click silently wrong.

32
00:01:38.333 --> 00:01:41.267
Next up: visual regression testing with AI.
